# Draft delivery lineage exported by the Proposal Workbench (BRSF software-development profile). Refine, then validate with the BRSF validator.

ex:Mission a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "Schedule quality checker for construction programmes using DCMA checks and SHACL rules"@en ; backlog:hasMissionStatement "Help the planning engineers of a construction project management firm review contractor programmes faster and more consistently. The project delivers a Python tool that reads a programme exported to Excel, checks it against twelve of the DCMA 14-point schedule quality checks written as SHACL rules, and produces an Excel report that lists every finding by activity. With this report, the planning engineer can send precise, rule-based comments to the contractor, and the project manager can accept a programme knowing that its logic, float and dates have been checked the same way every time." ; backlog:hasMissionOutcome "A planning engineer runs one command on the contractor's exported programme and, within a minute, receives an Excel report with a pass or fail for twelve DCMA checks and a list of every offending activity, ready to send back to the contractor, instead of filtering the schedule by hand." ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived .
ex:Lineage a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 .
ex:Customer1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Construction project management firm, planning and project controls team"@en ; rdfs:comment "Customer (client): A repeatable, documented quality check of every contractor programme in minutes, with a finding list it can send back to the contractor."@en .
ex:EndUser1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Planning engineer"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: planning engineers of the project management firm who review contractor programmes - exports the contractor's programme to the Excel template, runs the checker and reviews the findings before replying to the contractor (monthly, office laptop)"@en .
ex:EndUser2 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Project manager"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: project managers who accept or return a contractor's programme on behalf of the employer - reads the summary sheet of the report to decide whether the programme can be accepted (monthly, office laptop)"@en .
