ex:X1 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Recalculating the schedule (CPM), the critical path test and the critical path length index"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "they need the planning software's calculation engine; the values in the export are enough for the other twelve checks" .
ex:X2 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Reading XER, MPP or MS Project XML files directly"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "each format needs its own parser, and both P6 and MS Project can export the activity table to Excel" .
ex:X3 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Revision comparison, trend charts, a web interface and a database"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "checking one file at a time meets the need, and the tool is run by one engineer on one computer" .
ex:X4 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Correcting the programme or writing back to it"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "the reviewer must stay independent; corrections are the contractor's job" .
ex:X5 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Delay analysis and extension-of-time assessment"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "it needs expert and contractual judgement beyond rule checks" .
ex:X6 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Real project programmes in the repository"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "programmes are confidential; the repository holds synthetic files only" .
ex:G1 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Defective programmes are caught before they are accepted"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "this is the change the planning team needs" .
ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Every template column the checks need is read reliably"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "a column read wrongly would hide or invent findings" .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "The planning engineer receives a report ready to send to the contractor"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "the check is only useful if its result reaches the contractor" .
ex:G4 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "No work is spent outside the three scope areas"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "recalculation, file parsers and a web interface were left out to keep the project small" .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The tool reads a programme from the three-sheet Excel template (Project, Activities, Relationships), refuses a file whose required columns are missing and names them, and converts each value, accepting forms such as 12, 12d or 12 gün. It maps the programme to an RDF graph and validates it with SHACL shapes for checks 1 to 11 of the DCMA 14-point assessment; SPARQL queries compute each check's ratio and the baseline execution index. It writes an Excel report with a summary sheet (value, threshold and pass, fail or not applicable per check), a findings sheet with one row per finding, and a method sheet with the counting rules. Given a folder, it checks every file in parallel and adds one summary table. It never recalculates the schedule and never sends data outside the computer." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a defect-free synthetic programme of 200 activities, when the planning engineer runs the checker, then all twelve checks pass and the findings sheet is empty" .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a template whose Relationships sheet lacks the predecessor column, when the checker reads it, then it stops, names the missing column and writes no report" .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Boundary ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given an activity with exactly 44 working days of total float, when the checker runs, then check 6 reports no finding for it, and at 45 days it does" .
ex:Scen4 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Absent ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a programme with an empty baseline finish column, when the checker runs, then checks 11 and 14 are reported as not applicable rather than passed" .
ex:O1 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Seeded defects detected"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "share of the defects seeded into the synthetic test programmes that appear in the findings sheet" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0%" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "95%" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Template columns read without manual editing"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "required template columns the reader accepts in the sample files, out of 19" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "19" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Report sheets produced automatically"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "sheets of the audit report (summary, findings, method) written by the tool without manual editing" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "3" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O4 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Commits outside the scope areas"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G4 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "git log query counting commits that change files outside reader/, graph/, shapes/, report/, cli/ and tests/" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The planning engineer exports the contractor's programme to the template and starts the checker on a file or a folder. For a folder, each file is processed in its own thread. The reader opens the workbook; if a required sheet or column is missing it stops and reports it. Otherwise it cleans each value, and an unreadable cell is reported with its sheet and row. The rows are mapped to an RDF graph. pySHACL validates the graph against the shapes and SPARQL queries compute the ratios and the baseline execution index; if the baseline column is empty, checks 11 and 14 are marked not applicable. The report writer produces the Excel report, and for a folder the summary table." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The planning engineer calls the command-line tool with a path. The tool asks the Reader for the three sheets and receives rows or a list of missing columns. It sends the rows to the Mapper, which returns an RDF graph. It sends the graph and the shapes file to the Validator (pySHACL), which returns the validation report. It sends the graph to the Metrics module, which runs the SPARQL queries and returns one value per check. It passes the findings and values to the ReportWriter, which writes the Excel file and returns its path, and the tool prints the path for the engineer." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Project has a name and a data date and has many Activities. Activity has an id, name, type (task, milestone, level of effort, summary), status, duration, start, finish, actual start, actual finish, total float, constraint type, baseline finish and resource. Relationship links a predecessor Activity to a successor Activity and has a type (FS, SS, FF, SF) and a lag. Check has a number, a name, a threshold and a counting rule. Finding links one Check to one Activity or Relationship and has a measured value and a message. AuditReport belongs to one Project and holds a result per Check and many Findings." .
